# One row pair for the same from+kind: an unguarded fallback AND a guarded refinement — and the
# unguarded one is written FIRST on purpose. The format reads the guarded row as refining the
# unguarded one (QUESTIONS.md Q6), so the guarded row must win whenever its comparison passes,
# even though the file lists it second. A generator that emitted rows in file order would make
# `high` unreachable here, which is the whole reason this fixture exists.
version 1
machine RefinedPair
initial A
transition A --1--> B
transition A --1--> C when ge 10 action high
transition C --2--> A
